ty::misaligned-code

  × the code's region `CODE` starts at a misaligned address
    ╭─[chip_interrupts_misaligned_495_thumbv7m.ers:8:27]
  7 │ memory {
  8 │     region CODE { origin: 0x400, size: 0x1_0000 }
    ·                           ──┬──
    ·                             ╰── 0x400 is not a multiple of 2048
  9 │     region DATA { origin: 0x2000_0000, size: 0x1_0000 }
 10 │     code in CODE;
    ·     ──────┬─────
    ·           ╰── places the code, from the reset entry on, in `CODE`
